-- title:
--   Normality of a local domain with crossing-model completion
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a noetherian local commutative ring which is an integral domain, and let $W$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal. Let $\pi \in W$ be an irreducible element (that is, a uniformiser) and let $E$ be a natural number with $1 \le E$. Suppose there is an isomorphism of rings $\iota$ between the completion of $R$ along its maximal ideal, $\mathrm{AdicCompletion}(\mathfrak m_R, R)$, and the quotient of the ring of formal power series in two variables $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi^E)$, where $C$ is the constant-coefficient inclusion of $W$; this quotient is the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$, written `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)`. The conclusion is that $R$ is integrally closed: every element of the fraction field of $R$ which is integral over $R$ already lies in the image of $R$.
--
--   This is the normality criterion for a local ring whose completion is a crossing (ordinary double point over a discrete valuation ring) model, the form in which normality of integral models of modular curves at their crossing points is obtained. It is used in the analysis of node annuli and of ring layers attached to nodal curves, where integral closedness of the local rings in question is needed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_isIntegrallyClosed_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open ModularCurve

theorem IsLocalRing.isIntegrallyClosed_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {W : Type*} [CommRing W] [IsDomain W] [IsDiscreteValuationRing W]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal W) W]
    (π : W) (hπ : Irreducible π) (E : ℕ) (hE : 1 ≤ E)
    (ι : AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R ≃+* UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed R := by sorry
